<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bankruptcies up yr/yr 27 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Belgian bankruptcies up yr/yr 27 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company bankruptcies in Belgium rose by 27 percent to 681 in April compared with April 1997, Belgian trade and company data group Infotrade said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In the first four months of 1997 a total of 2,828 companies went bankrupt, up 14 percent from 2,472 in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>Infotrade said 1,600 jobs had been lost as a result of the bankruptcies.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
